 # bench-workspace-ya (benchmark fixture)
 
-A workspace-browser replacement plugin: the bundle patch disables the
-official `ui-workspace` client entry and the browser half registers the
-replacement two-level sidebar (`sidebar.workspaces`) plus the conversation
-hero picker (`conversation.hero.workspace`), written in the 0.1.1-era style.
-The host is moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+A workspace-browser replacement plugin for dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2: the bundle patch
+disables the official `ui-workspace` client entry and the browser half registers
+the replacement two-level sidebar (`sidebar.workspaces`) plus the conversation
+hero picker (`conversation.hero.workspace`), together with both
+`*.directoryFlow` child holes the composed directory pickers fill.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+- Browser half: cordis `inject` is `slots`, `sessions`, `workspaces`,
+  `uiWorkspace`, `locale`; navigation goes through the official
+  `ctx.uiWorkspace` service, and reads use the global `useWorkspaces` hook.
+- Those two shared roles must survive disabling the `ui-workspace` row, so this
+  plugin needs a harness release whose web bundle mounts the separate
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace-navigation` entry. Without it, the
+  official `uiWorkspace` consumers stay pending and the web boot fails with
+  `web boot: N entries did not activate`.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
